<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" class="icon icon-tabler icons-tabler-filled icon-tabler-user">
<!-- Bust, the mark for a BOUNTY task, drawn inside the task reticle rather than in a
     badge ring. Tabler Icons user-filled (MIT).

     BYTE-IDENTICAL TO svg/vip.svg TODAY, and copied rather than referenced so the two
     can diverge without either changing by surprise. The same glyph marks two very
     different things, and that is deliberate:

       vip     bust in a BADGE RING, purple (190,140,240) or companion green
       bounty  bust in the TASK RETICLE, red (214,44,60)

     The frame separates them before the colour does. A ring badge means "a person who
     is here"; the reticle means "a task, go and find it", which is the same grammar
     the mutant skull uses. Filled rather than outline, for the reason recorded in
     skull.svg: at the 26 px a minimap spot gets, an outline glyph is nearly all
     keyline and a mark's apparent colour is the mean over its own area.

     If the two ever do read as one thing on the map, change THIS file, not vip.svg.
     Everything the bounty needs in order to stay distinct is here. -->
<path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z" fill="none" /><path d="M12 2a5 5 0 1 1 -5 5l.005 -.217a5 5 0 0 1 4.995 -4.783z" /><path d="M14 14a5 5 0 0 1 5 5v1a2 2 0 0 1 -2 2h-10a2 2 0 0 1 -2 -2v-1a5 5 0 0 1 5 -5h4z" /></svg>
